<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    THE TOWER FLOORS.

    Separate from the colony dungeons and marked towerOnly, so the two pools
    never mix: DungeonKindSelector skips these, TowerLadder requires them.

    ONE THEME PER FLOOR. This is the rule the first version of this file broke.
    Its rosters were built as the UNION of everything the gate dungeons used
    across each rank band, which produced floors holding wyverns, liches,
    demons, hell ogres and dragons all at once - a bestiary, not a place. A
    floor should read as somewhere with an occupant, so each draws from one
    theme and nothing else:

      warrens      greenskins        kobolds, goblins
      ossuary      the undead        skeletons, liches, shamblers
      furnace      the infernal      imps, demons
      infested     flesh horrors     Anomaly entities
      necropolis   the undead, late
      pits         the infernal, late
      grove        the verdant       treants, dryads
      warcamp      greenskins, late  orcs
      coldreach    the primal        trolls, minotaurs
      cinderwaste  the draconic      wyverns, dragons
      choir        the celestial     Empire soldiery, valkyries, archangels
      plains       peaceful          roster suppressed by the archetype
      grotto       slimes, early     crystalline slimes
      hollows      the swarm         megascarabs, spelopedes, megaspiders
      hold         greenskins, mid   orcs, and the trolls they work
      machineworks the mechanoid     lancers, centipedes, diaboli

    A theme may appear TWICE, early and late, and several do - the warrens
    and the warcamp, the ossuary and the necropolis, the furnace and the
    pits. What the rule forbids is two themes on ONE floor, not one theme on
    two floors. A climber should recognise where they are and still be able
    to tell floor 12 from floor 62.

    THE CELESTIAL PROBLEM, and why the Empire is up there. The mod ships
    exactly two celestial creatures - one valkyrie, one archangel - which is
    not a roster. That scarcity is precisely why valkyries used to leak into
    demon crypts and misty trenches: there was nothing else to stand beside
    them. Royalty Empire troopers are gold-armoured elite humanlikes, which is
    what a celestial host soldiery should look like, so the summit borrows them
    and the valkyrie goes back to being the rare thing.

    requiresFullRoster is TRUE wherever the roster is all base-mod creatures,
    and FALSE only where DLC content is mixed in - so a player without Anomaly,
    Ideology or Royalty loses those entries rather than losing the floor.
  -->

  <IsekaiDungeons.DungeonKindDef ParentName="IsekaiDungeonBase">
    <defName>IsekaiDungeons_Tower_Warren_F</defName>
    <label>the warrens</label>
    <description>The lowest floors were colonised a long time ago by things small enough to fit through the gaps. They have dug their own passages off the tower corridors, and they are not frightened of you yet.</description>
    <towerOnly>true</towerOnly>

    <mapGenerator>IsekaiDungeons_Dungeon</mapGenerator>
    <minRank>F</minRank>
    <maxRank>D</maxRank>
    <selectionWeight>1.0</selectionWeight>

    <layoutMode>Carve</layoutMode>
    <roofed>true</roofed>
    <floorTerrain>IsekaiDungeons_SanctumStone</floorTerrain>
    <roster>
      <li><kind>IsekaiKobold_Pup</kind><weight>1.4</weight></li>
      <li><kind>IsekaiKobold_Slinger</kind><weight>1.2</weight></li>
      <li><kind>IsekaiGoblin_Runt</kind><weight>1.2</weight></li>
      <li><kind>IsekaiGoblin_Slinger</kind><weight>1.0</weight></li>
      <li><kind>IsekaiKobold_Warrior</kind><weight>0.9</weight><minDepth>0.35</minDepth></li>
      <li><kind>IsekaiGoblin_Warrior</kind><weight>0.9</weight><minDepth>0.45</minDepth></li>
      <li><kind>IsekaiKobold_Archer</kind><weight>0.7</weight><minDepth>0.6</minDepth></li>
    </roster>
    <bosses>
      <li>IsekaiKobold_Chieftain</li>
      <li>IsekaiGoblin_Hobgoblin</li>
    </bosses>
    <requiresFullRoster>true</requiresFullRoster>
  </IsekaiDungeons.DungeonKindDef>

  <IsekaiDungeons.DungeonKindDef ParentName="IsekaiDungeonBase">
    <defName>IsekaiDungeons_Tower_Ossuary_D</defName>
    <label>the ossuary floors</label>
    <description>Everyone who died on the way up is still here, and the tower has kept them tidy. The alcoves are full, and the things standing in them have had a very long time to get used to standing.</description>
    <towerOnly>true</towerOnly>

    <mapGenerator>IsekaiDungeons_Crypt</mapGenerator>
    <minRank>D</minRank>
    <maxRank>B</maxRank>
    <selectionWeight>1.0</selectionWeight>

    <layoutMode>Carve</layoutMode>
    <roofed>true</roofed>
    <floorTerrain>IsekaiDungeons_SanctumStone</floorTerrain>
    <roster>
      <li><kind>IsekaiSkeleton_Common</kind><weight>1.4</weight></li>
      <li><kind>ShamblerSwarmer</kind><weight>1.0</weight></li>
      <li><kind>IsekaiSkeleton_Goblin</kind><weight>1.1</weight><minDepth>0.25</minDepth></li>
      <li><kind>ShamblerSoldier</kind><weight>0.9</weight><minDepth>0.4</minDepth></li>
      <li><kind>IsekaiSkeleton_Orc</kind><weight>0.8</weight><minDepth>0.55</minDepth></li>
      <li><kind>Gorehulk</kind><weight>0.6</weight><minDepth>0.7</minDepth></li>
    </roster>
    <bosses>
      <!-- A ladder, not alternatives: the band guard filters this list to what
           the floor's rank can carry (rank + 1), so a D floor is crowned by
           the skeleton goblin [C], a C floor by the skeleton orc [B], and only
           the top of the band ever meets the lich [A]. Before the guard the
           list rolled blind, which put that A-rank lich on D floors - the
           "liches on the first floors" bug. -->
      <li>IsekaiLich_Adult</li>
      <li>IsekaiSkeleton_Orc</li>
      <li>IsekaiSkeleton_Goblin</li>
