  <IsekaiDungeons.DungeonKindDef ParentName="IsekaiDungeonBase">
    <defName>IsekaiDungeons_Tower_Plains</defName>
    <label>the plains</label>
    <description>Open grassland under a sky the tower has no business having. There are trees, there is running water somewhere out of sight, and the animals watch you go past without much interest.</description>
    <towerOnly>true</towerOnly>

    <mapGenerator>IsekaiDungeons_TowerPlains</mapGenerator>
    <minRank>E</minRank>
    <maxRank>SSS</maxRank>
    <!-- PINNED, so this is reachable ONLY from the two archetypes that name
         it: the plains floor and the market floor.

         The header calls the plains roster "suppressed by the archetype", and
         that is the whole design - a calm floor and a village floor, neither
         of which spawns it. But nothing enforced it. Any archetype that
         allowed Open could roll the plains as an ordinary fight, and its
         roster is three small slimes, so above rank C every one of them falls
         outside the band, the roster comes back empty, and the floor drops to
         the generic rank-banded providers. That is a floor holding whatever
         the tier happens to contain: the bestiary-instead-of-a-place failure
         this file was rewritten to stop.

         It is pinned rather than merely down-weighted because down-weighting
         makes a wrong floor rarer, and rare is the worse failure - it becomes
         the bug nobody can reproduce. selectionWeight is left at 0 to say the
         same thing twice: a pin ignores it, so any value would be dead text,
         and a zero cannot quietly resurrect this if the pin is ever removed. -->
    <selectionWeight>0</selectionWeight>
    <pinnedOnly>true</pinnedOnly>

    <layoutMode>Open</layoutMode>
    <openZoneRadiusRange><min>9</min><max>16</max></openZoneRadiusRange>
    <roster>
      <li><kind>IsekaiSlime_Blue_Small</kind><weight>1.0</weight></li>
      <li><kind>IsekaiSlime_Green_Small</kind><weight>1.0</weight></li>
      <li><kind>IsekaiSlime_Blue_Medium</kind><weight>0.6</weight><minDepth>0.5</minDepth></li>
    </roster>
    <bosses>
      <li>IsekaiSlime_Metal_Large</li>
    </bosses>
    <requiresFullRoster>true</requiresFullRoster>
  </IsekaiDungeons.DungeonKindDef>


  <!--
    FLOOR 50 - THE MIRROR HALL. Halfway up, the tower fights back with YOU.

    One giant pillared chamber; the population is a locked character-forge
    copy of every colonist who walks in (see DungeonKindDef.mirrorArena and
    MirrorArena.cs). No roster, no bosses list - the party brings its own.

    Band F-Nation on purpose: this def is PINNED to floor 50 by its archetype,
    and a band that could ever exclude the floor's rolled rank would break the
    pin (TowerLadder refuses out-of-band pins loudly). The rank only feeds the
    loot payout - the fight's difficulty IS the player's own roster.
  -->
  <IsekaiDungeons.DungeonKindDef ParentName="IsekaiDungeonBase">
    <defName>IsekaiDungeons_Tower_MirrorHall_50</defName>
    <label>the mirror hall</label>
    <description>A single vaulted chamber, colonnades marching into the dark, polished floor like still water. Nothing lives here. The tower does not need anything to live here - whoever walks in supplies both sides of the fight.</description>
    <towerOnly>true</towerOnly>
    <mirrorArena>true</mirrorArena>

    <mapGenerator>IsekaiDungeons_MirrorArena</mapGenerator>
    <objectiveWorkerClass>IsekaiDungeons.DungeonObjectiveWorker_MirrorArena</objectiveWorkerClass>

    <minRank>F</minRank>
    <maxRank>SSS</maxRank>
    <!-- pinnedOnly is what actually keeps this off other floors: a weight of
         0 does NOT, because PickDungeon floors every weight at 0.01. -->
    <selectionWeight>0</selectionWeight>

    <layoutMode>Carve</layoutMode>
    <pinnedOnly>true</pinnedOnly>
    <roofed>true</roofed>
    <floorTerrain>IsekaiDungeons_SanctumStone</floorTerrain>

    <!-- The hall is 57 cells plus the alcove; 150 leaves a thick rock margin
         all round while keeping the pocket map cheap to tick. -->
    <mapSizeByRank>
      <points>
        <li>(0, 150)</li>
        <li>(9, 150)</li>
      </points>
    </mapSizeByRank>

    <!-- No roster and no requirement for one: the def is available on every
         install because its population is the player's own party. -->
    <requiresFullRoster>false</requiresFullRoster>
    <bossIsElite>false</bossIsElite>
  </IsekaiDungeons.DungeonKindDef>


  <!--
    FLOOR 100 - THE SUMMIT. Open ground under a sky that is not yours, which
    is exactly how the summit letter has always described it, and Elijah
    standing on it.

    authoredBoss replaces the rolled boss with the character def, and bossOnly
    empties the rest of the floor: no approach, no escort, nothing between the
    stair and her. She has held this roof alone for five centuries and an
    honour guard contradicts every line of that - it also buried the one thing
    the floor exists for. Band S-Nation because the ladder puts floor 100 at
    rank 9 and the archetype pins this def outright.
  -->
  <IsekaiDungeons.DungeonKindDef ParentName="IsekaiDungeonBase">
    <defName>IsekaiDungeons_Tower_Summit_100</defName>
    <label>the summit</label>
    <description>There is no ceiling here and no stair onward - just open ground, a horizon that does not behave, and one figure standing on it who has been standing on it for a very long time. She does not appear to be waiting for anything in particular. She simply has not been relieved.</description>
    <towerOnly>true</towerOnly>

    <!-- Its own generator: the Celestial field minus the ruins and plants. -->
    <mapGenerator>IsekaiDungeons_Summit</mapGenerator>
    <authoredBoss>IsekaiDungeons_Elijah</authoredBoss>

    <minRank>S</minRank>
    <maxRank>SSS</maxRank>
    <!-- Never rolled: the archetype pins it. -->
    <selectionWeight>0</selectionWeight>

    <!-- OPEN, not Build. Build is the walled-compound mode that no shipped
         dungeon uses, and it would put the final duel inside a corridor
         complex; Open leaves the map untouched, which is the "open ground
         under a sky that is not yours" the summit letter has always
         described. Every other Celestial dungeon is Open too. -->
    <layoutMode>Open</layoutMode>
    <pinnedOnly>true</pinnedOnly>

    <!-- ELIJAH, ALONE. No roster: bossOnly suppresses the population pass
         outright, so an empty list here is the honest statement of it rather
         than a list that happens never to be read. -->
    <bossOnly>true</bossOnly>
    <requiresFullRoster>false</requiresFullRoster>
    <bossIsElite>false</bossIsElite>
  </IsekaiDungeons.DungeonKindDef>

  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       THE FLOORS ADDED TO BREAK THE MONOCULTURE.

       Everything above this line was written band by band, and the bands
       happened to leave holes: rank F had ONE indoor floor in the whole
       catalogue and rank A had two, while the indoor archetypes carry three
       quarters of the tower. A climber at floor 50 met the same two places
       over and over, which is a content shortage wearing a scheduling bug's
       clothes - and fixing only the scheduling would just have spread two
       environments more evenly.

       These four are deliberately built from generators and creature
       families the mod ALREADY ships and the tower never used: the plain
       stone dungeon above rank D, the insect hive, and the mechanoids, who
       did not appear anywhere in the tower at all. No new art, no new
       pawns - the gap was never in the content, only in the catalogue.
       ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->

  <!-- F..C indoor. The tower's low water table, and the answer to rank F
       having exactly one indoor floor - which made floors 1-3 the same place
       every single game. Crystalline slimes rather than the field slimes of
       the plains: same family, and read as a different room. -->
  <IsekaiDungeons.DungeonKindDef ParentName="IsekaiDungeonBase">
    <defName>IsekaiDungeons_Tower_Grotto_F</defName>
    <label>the seeping floors</label>
    <description>Water has got in, and it has been getting in for a long time. The stone is furred with something soft that holds the light, and the light bends wrong on the way through. Every surface here is faintly, patiently wet.</description>
    <towerOnly>true</towerOnly>

    <mapGenerator>IsekaiDungeons_Dungeon</mapGenerator>
    <minRank>F</minRank>
    <maxRank>C</maxRank>
    <selectionWeight>1.0</selectionWeight>

    <layoutMode>Carve</layoutMode>
    <roofed>true</roofed>
    <floorTerrain>IsekaiDungeons_SanctumStone</floorTerrain>
    <roster>
      <li><kind>IsekaiSlime_Sky_Small</kind><weight>1.3</weight></li>
      <li><kind>IsekaiSlime_Green_Small</kind><weight>1.1</weight></li>
      <li><kind>IsekaiSlime_Yellow_Medium</kind><weight>1.0</weight><minDepth>0.25</minDepth></li>
      <li><kind>IsekaiSlime_Sky_Medium</kind><weight>0.9</weight><minDepth>0.40</minDepth></li>
      <li><kind>IsekaiSlime_Red_Medium</kind><weight>0.8</weight><minDepth>0.55</minDepth></li>
      <li><kind>IsekaiSlime_Metal_Medium</kind><weight>0.6</weight><minDepth>0.70</minDepth></li>
    </roster>
    <bosses>
      <li>IsekaiSlime_Sky_Large</li>
      <li>IsekaiSlime_Metal_Large</li>
    </bosses>
    <requiresFullRoster>true</requiresFullRoster>
  </IsekaiDungeons.DungeonKindDef>

  <!-- E..C indoor. Insects, which the tower never had. requiresFullRoster is
       true and safe: every kind here is base RimWorld, so there is no install
       on which this roster can come up short. -->
  <IsekaiDungeons.DungeonKindDef ParentName="IsekaiDungeonBase">
    <defName>IsekaiDungeons_Tower_Hollows_E</defName>
    <label>the hollow floors</label>
    <description>Something chewed these passages rather than cutting them, and it did not care where the tower wanted walls. The floor crunches. The sound carries a great deal further than it should, and it goes both ways.</description>
    <towerOnly>true</towerOnly>

    <mapGenerator>IsekaiDungeons_Hive</mapGenerator>
    <minRank>E</minRank>
    <maxRank>C</maxRank>
    <selectionWeight>1.0</selectionWeight>

    <layoutMode>Carve</layoutMode>
    <roofed>true</roofed>
    <floorTerrain>IsekaiDungeons_SanctumStone</floorTerrain>
    <roster>
      <li><kind>Megascarab</kind><weight>1.4</weight></li>
      <li><kind>Spelopede</kind><weight>1.0</weight><minDepth>0.25</minDepth></li>
      <li><kind>Megaspider</kind><weight>0.7</weight><minDepth>0.50</minDepth></li>
    </roster>
    <bosses>
      <li>Megaspider</li>
      <li>Spelopede</li>
    </bosses>
    <requiresFullRoster>true</requiresFullRoster>
  </IsekaiDungeons.DungeonKindDef>

  <!-- C..A indoor. THE RANK-A HOLE. Above rank B the indoor catalogue was the
       furnace and the fleshworks and nothing else, which is the floor range a
       long campaign spends the most time in.

       Orcs get their own floor here rather than sharing the warcamp's. The
       warcamp is a surface camp of orcs and goblins together in the D..B
       band; this is what the orcs built once they stopped camping. -->
  <IsekaiDungeons.DungeonKindDef ParentName="IsekaiDungeonBase">
    <defName>IsekaiDungeons_Tower_Deeps_C</defName>
    <label>the hold floors</label>
    <description>Someone has been improving the tower's work. The passages have been widened, squared and braced, and there are doors on them - heavy ones, hung properly, and hung from the far side.</description>
    <towerOnly>true</towerOnly>

    <mapGenerator>IsekaiDungeons_Dungeon</mapGenerator>
    <minRank>C</minRank>
    <maxRank>A</maxRank>
    <selectionWeight>1.0</selectionWeight>

    <layoutMode>Carve</layoutMode>
    <roofed>true</roofed>
    <floorTerrain>IsekaiDungeons_SanctumStone</floorTerrain>
    <roster>
      <li><kind>IsekaiOrc_Whelp</kind><weight>1.3</weight></li>
      <li><kind>IsekaiOrc_Warrior</kind><weight>1.1</weight></li>
      <li><kind>IsekaiSkeleton_Orc</kind><weight>0.8</weight></li>
      <li><kind>IsekaiTroll_Baby</kind><weight>0.9</weight><minDepth>0.25</minDepth></li>
      <li><kind>IsekaiTroll_Adult</kind><weight>0.8</weight><minDepth>0.45</minDepth></li>
      <li><kind>IsekaiTroll_Upper</kind><weight>0.5</weight><minDepth>0.70</minDepth></li>
    </roster>
    <bosses>
      <li>IsekaiOrc_Warlord</li>
      <li>IsekaiTroll_Upper</li>
    </bosses>
    <requiresFullRoster>true</requiresFullRoster>
  </IsekaiDungeons.DungeonKindDef>

  <!-- B..SSS indoor. Mechanoids, who appeared NOWHERE in the tower despite
       the mod shipping five mechanoid dungeons for the colony pool. The
       widest band in the file on purpose: it is the only thing standing
       between rank S and a two-environment stretch, and a machine floor is
       the one enemy set here that does not care what rank it is fighting.

       requiresFullRoster FALSE because most of these are Biotech - per the
       rule at the top of the file, a player without the DLC loses the
       entries rather than the floor. -->
  <IsekaiDungeons.DungeonKindDef ParentName="IsekaiDungeonBase">
    <defName>IsekaiDungeons_Tower_Machineworks_B</defName>
    <label>the machine floors</label>
    <description>This course was fitted out, not occupied. The walls carry conduit that still hums, the lighting is even, and nothing here has decayed by so much as a hinge. Whatever installed all this has never stopped maintaining it.</description>
    <towerOnly>true</towerOnly>

    <mapGenerator>IsekaiDungeons_Dungeon</mapGenerator>
    <minRank>B</minRank>
    <maxRank>SSS</maxRank>
    <selectionWeight>1.0</selectionWeight>

    <layoutMode>Carve</layoutMode>
    <roofed>true</roofed>
    <floorTerrain>IsekaiDungeons_SanctumStone</floorTerrain>
    <roster>
      <li><kind>Mech_Lancer</kind><weight>1.2</weight></li>
      <li><kind>Mech_Scyther</kind><weight>1.1</weight></li>
      <li><kind>Mech_CentipedeGunner</kind><weight>0.9</weight></li>
      <li><kind>Mech_CentipedeBlaster</kind><weight>0.8</weight><minDepth>0.30</minDepth></li>
      <li><kind>Mech_Legionary</kind><weight>0.7</weight><minDepth>0.45</minDepth></li>
      <li><kind>Mech_CentipedeBurner</kind><weight>0.6</weight><minDepth>0.60</minDepth></li>
      <li><kind>Mech_Termite_Breach</kind><weight>0.5</weight><minDepth>0.75</minDepth></li>
    </roster>
    <bosses>
      <li>Mech_Diabolus</li>
      <li>Mech_Apocriton</li>
      <li>Mech_Warqueen</li>
    </bosses>
    <requiresFullRoster>false</requiresFullRoster>
  </IsekaiDungeons.DungeonKindDef>

</Defs>
